WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:06.040
Causematch matches people with nonprofits across Los Angeles County that need a hand.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.400
Here's how a new nonprofit and a new volunteer find each other.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.066
First, a nonprofit joins.

00:00:13.066 --> 00:00:20.380
Jordan, from Silver Lake Garden Friends, asks for access with the organization's name and tax ID.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:26.042
A Causematch admin reviews the request and approves it in one tap.

00:00:26.042 --> 00:00:28.900
Jordan gets an email with a sign-in link.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.872
There's no password to remember.

00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:37.030
Jordan enters their email, opens the link, and lands on an empty dashboard.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.456
Jordan says the nonprofit can confirm volunteer hours.

00:00:41.456 --> 00:00:49.560
Then Jordan posts an opening: what volunteers will do, where and when, how long it lasts, and how many people they need.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.279
Now, a volunteer.

00:01:04.279 --> 00:01:09.270
Riley signs up with a phone number and the six-digit code we text them.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:16.930
One short form: a first name, where Riley will help from, and how much they care about each cause.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:26.465
In preferences, under When, Riley ticks the times they're usually free.

00:01:26.465 --> 00:01:27.740
These stay private.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.790
The deck ranks openings for Riley, and each card says why it's shown.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:40.304
Jordan's garden opening is right here.

00:01:40.304 --> 00:01:43.787
Riley taps the heart, and likes one more opening too.

00:01:43.787 --> 00:01:47.140
A like becomes a match when the nonprofit says yes.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.307
On Jordan's side, the inbox badge goes up.

00:01:53.307 --> 00:01:56.660
Riley appears with only what they chose to share.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.135
Jordan accepts and says hi.

00:01:59.135 --> 00:02:03.820
The first shift is booked, and on Riley's phone, right there: it's a match.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:09.460
Riley taps Say hi on the match, reads Jordan's message, and replies.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:16.140
The reply arrives live, and Jordan's dashboard flags it as a message to answer.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:21.790
And the shift is on Jordan's schedule, ready to mark attended once it happens.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.015
A few days later, the shift is done.

00:02:25.015 --> 00:02:30.180
Jordan marks Riley as attended in one tap, with the hours already filled in.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:34.098
Matches, with the likes still waiting below them.

00:02:34.098 --> 00:02:42.880
Then Riley opens Me, then Shifts and hours, and sees the hours the nonprofit confirmed: the shift, the nonprofit, and who confirmed them.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:48.010
For a certificate, Riley first adds a last name on the profile.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:03:00.490
Then, in Shifts and hours, Riley picks all hours and gets a certificate for Silver Lake Garden Friends: every confirmed shift, the total, a signature code, and a PDF with a QR code.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:05.829
Anyone with the link can check that it's genuine, with no sign-in.

00:03:05.829 --> 00:03:09.770
Same nonprofit, same total, unchanged since it was issued.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:16.945
In preferences, under Causes and places, Riley ticks, I need my hours confirmed, for school.

00:03:16.945 --> 00:03:20.751
Now the deck shows only nonprofits that confirm hours.

00:03:20.751 --> 00:03:23.380
Their cards say, Confirms your hours.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:25.863
Causematch.

00:03:25.863 --> 00:03:27.540
Swipe to volunteer.
